<div class='field-analysis matrix-analysis'>
  <div class='matrix-scroll' tabindex='0' role='region' aria-label='Matrix answer distribution'>
    <table class='matrix-summary'>
      <caption>Responses by statement and answer option</caption>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope='col'>Statement</th>
          <th scope='col'>Answered (n)</th>
          {% for label in columns %}
            <th scope='col'><span>{{ label }}</span></th>
          {% endfor %}
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {% for row in rows %}
          <tr>
            <th scope='row'>{{ row.label }}</th>
            <td class='matrix-n'>{{ "{:,}".format(row.denominator) }}</td>
            {% for cell in row.cells %}
              {% if cell.count is none %}
                <td class='matrix-cell unavailable' title='No exported option for this row'>—</td>
              {% else %}
                <td class='matrix-cell{% if not cell.count %} option-zero{% endif %}'>
                  <b>{{ "{:,}".format(cell.count) }}</b><small>{{ cell.percentage }}</small>
                  <span class='matrix-meter' aria-hidden='true'><i style='width:{{ cell.width }}'></i></span>
                </td>
              {% endif %}
            {% endfor %}
          </tr>
        {% endfor %}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p class='meta'>Each cell shows a respondent count and percentage of respondents who answered that row. Answer options follow the survey definition order. Multiple selections can total more than 100%. A missing answer does not tell us whether the question was shown. — means no row responses or no exported option for that row.</p>
</div>
